{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.CommutativeImageDegeneration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.CommutativeImageDegeneration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Span","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.operator_basis_degenerates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.operator_basis_degenerates","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L136-L154","doc":"**The degeneration theorem.** In any commutative image, all six\nGröbner–Shirshov basis operators of `H₃(q)` — `1`, `σ₀`, `σ₁`, `L₊`, `L₋`,\n`e⁻` — lie in `span R {1, s}`, and `σ₀ = σ₁`, `L₊ = L₋`.\n\nA six-dimensional operator algebra with an at-most-two-dimensional image: the\nparticle catalogue's distinctions do not survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cube_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cube_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L124-L134","doc":"`s³` lies in `span R {1, s}` too: `s³ = (q − qi)·s² + s`, and `s²` is\nalready in the span. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.sq_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.sq_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L115-L122","doc":"`s²` lies in `span R {1, s}` — directly the quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.braid_forces_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.braid_forces_eq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L92-L107","doc":"**The braid relation collapses the two generators.**\n\nIn a commutative target the braid relation `σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁` reads\n`s₀²s₁ = s₁²s₀`, i.e. `s₀s₁(s₀ − s₁) = 0`; both factors are units by\n`isUnit_of_heckeQuad`, so `s₀ = s₁`.\n\nThis is the first half of the degeneration, and it needs **only** the braid\nrelation plus the quadratic — no eigenvalue case split, no domain, no\nconjugacy argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.eq_or_eq_of_heckeQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.eq_or_eq_of_heckeQuad","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L83-L90","doc":"**Two eigenvalues, in a domain.** The classical statement: a Hecke\ngenerator acts by `q` or by `-q⁻¹` — the symmetric and antisymmetric channels\nof AGENTS.md §7a. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.heckeQuad_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.heckeQuad_factor","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L75-L81","doc":"The Hecke quadratic in factored form: `(s - q) * (s + qi) = 0`, given\n`q * qi = 1`. Valid over any `CommRing` — the *disjunction* `s = q ∨ s = -qi`\nneeds a domain and is `eq_or_eq_of_heckeQuad` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.isUnit_of_heckeQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.isUnit_of_heckeQuad","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**Every Hecke generator is a unit.** Immediate from the quadratic:\n`s * (s - (q - qi)) = 1`. This is what makes the cancellation in\n`braid_forces_eq` legitimate without any domain hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.HeckeQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.HeckeQuad","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/CommutativeImageDegeneration.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The Hecke quadratic relation in the form `s² = (q − q⁻¹)·s + 1`, carrying\nthe inverse as an explicit element `qi` so the statement lives over a plain\n`CommRing` (AGENTS.md §7c: no gratuitous field or `ℝ`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}